From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: sunxi: no host side where the phy routes host mode away

Megi's "Avoid enabling host side code on SoCs where it's not used"
(orange-pi-7.3, 2916a0f5bdec): on the A64 (and H3, R40, V3s, H6) host mode
on PHY 0 is EHCI0/OHCI0's, the PHY routing the port to them, so MUSB is
peripheral only. And, beyond his: a host notification (the role switch,
0042) leaves MUSB idle rather than an A-device waiting for VBUS with a
session: after a dock was replugged it sat in a_wait_vrise beside EHCI0,
which had the port. (It did not fix a dock's full-speed mouse receiver
timing out on EHCI0: that one needs replugging, see 0046.)

Peripheral only, the glue's phy mode is the device's too: left at OTG (the
PinePhone's dr_mode with its role switch, 0044), musb_init_controller()
asked for the peripheral mode, sunxi_musb_set_mode() refused to change it
on a port not dual role, and the probe failed: no gadget, and the first
suspend oopsed in the firmware loader's notifier (devres_for_each_res()).

---
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
@@ -110,7 +110,13 @@
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&musb->lock, flags);
 
 		devctl = readb(musb->mregs + SUNXI_MUSB_DEVCTL);
-		if (test_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_HOSTMODE, &glue->flags)) {
+		/*
+		 * Peripheral only (the phy routes host mode to EHCI/OHCI, below):
+		 * left idle, not waiting for VBUS as an A-device with a session
+		 * on the phy the host controllers use meanwhile
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_HOSTMODE, &glue->flags) &&
+		    musb->port_mode != MUSB_PERIPHERAL) {
 			set_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_VBUS_ON, &glue->flags);
 			musb->xceiv->otg->state = OTG_STATE_A_WAIT_VRISE;
 			MUSB_HST_MODE(musb);
@@ -674,12 +680,21 @@
 	.ram_bits	= SUNXI_MUSB_RAM_BITS,
 };
 
+static const char * const sunxi_musb_host_rerouted_phys[] = {
+	"allwinner,sun8i-h3-usb-phy",
+	"allwinner,sun8i-r40-usb-phy",
+	"allwinner,sun8i-v3s-usb-phy",
+	"allwinner,sun50i-a64-usb-phy",
+	"allwinner,sun50i-h6-usb-phy",
+	NULL,
+};
+
 static int sunxi_musb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct musb_hdrc_platform_data	pdata;
 	struct platform_device_info	pinfo;
 	struct sunxi_glue		*glue;
-	struct device_node		*np = pdev->dev.of_node;
+	struct device_node		*np = pdev->dev.of_node, *phy_np;
 	const struct sunxi_musb_cfg	*cfg;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -761,6 +776,25 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(glue->phy),
 				     "Error getting phy\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * Host mode is handled outside of the musb driver on some allwinner
+	 * SoCs. We don't need musb host side code to be enabled at all.
+	 * In fact it causes occasional issues with suspend to ram, when
+	 * the host side code is enabled and unused (due to phy being re-routed
+	 * to a different *HCI controller).
+	 */
+	phy_np = glue->phy->dev.of_node;
+	if (of_device_compatible_match(phy_np, sunxi_musb_host_rerouted_phys)) {
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev, "Disabling musb host side code due to re-routed phy\n");
+		pdata.mode = MUSB_PERIPHERAL;
+		/*
+		 * And the phy mode it asks for: with dr_mode "otg" (a role
+		 * switch's port) musb_init_controller()'s set_mode found
+		 * another one and failed the probe
+		 */
+		glue->phy_mode = PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE;
+	}
+
 	glue->usb_phy = usb_phy_generic_register();
 	if (IS_ERR(glue->usb_phy)) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Error registering usb-phy %ld\n",
